  "body": {
    "id": "lem:scalar-airy-tube-zero-face-diagnostic",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(n,k\\geq1\\) and rational \\(\\varepsilon>0\\) for which the scalar subprior is admissible,\n\\[\n G_{n,k,\\varepsilon}^{\\dagger,\\mathrm A,0}(n,0,0)\n \\geq \\frac{11}{8}\\int_{\\mathbb R}|x|w_k^\\dagger(x)\\,dx\n\\frac{45}{256}\\varepsilon.\n\\]\nConsequently, if \\(k_n\\to\\infty\\),\n\\[\n \\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}\n G_{n,k_n,\\varepsilon_n}^{\\dagger,\\mathrm A,0}(n,0,0)\n \\geq\\frac{22}{15}\\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}>\n \\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}.\n\\]\nThus the scalar subprior cannot furnish the zero-face part of a sharp all-count converse; the added common-shift coordinate is load-bearing.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "k",
      "\\varepsilon",
      "w_k^\\dagger",
      "c^\\dagger",
      "G_{n,k,\\varepsilon}^{\\dagger,\\mathrm A,0}(r)",
      "\\Lambda_c",
      "r"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "prop:unequal-three-arm-exact-primitives",
      "def:airy-benchmark",
      "def:rational-airy-longitudinal-family",
      "lem:effective-normalized-airy-record",
      "def:scalar-airy-tube-legacy",
      "def:exact-scalar-airy-tube-bayes-risk"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Under allocation \\((n,0,0)\\), set\n\\(\\widetilde\\tau_n=n^{-1}\\sum_i(2Y_i^{\\mathrm{obs}}-1)\\) and\n\\(e(t)=2t_1-1-(c^\\dagger)^\\top t\\).  The exact target identity gives\n\\(\\widetilde\\tau_n-\\tau_{c^\\dagger}(m)=n^{-1}\\sum_ie(t_i)\\).  In lexicographic type order,\n\\[\n e(t)^2=(1,1/16,9/16,0,0,9/16,1/16,1).\n\\]\nThe scalar construction and the explicit response measures give\n\\[\n \\mathbb E[e(t)\\mid x,h]=0,\n \\qquad\n \\mathbb E[e(t)^2\\mid x,h]\n =1-\\alpha_n\\left(\\frac{11}{8}|x|+\\frac9{16}|h|\\right).\n\\]\nConditional independence therefore makes the risk of \\(\\widetilde\\tau_n\\)\n\\[\n \\frac1n-n^{-4/3}\\left\\{\n \\frac{11}{8}\\int|x|w_k^\\dagger(x)\\,dx\n\\frac9{16}\\int|h|\\rho_\\varepsilon(h)\\,dh\\right\\}.\n\\]\nDirect integration yields\n\\(\\int|h|\\rho_\\varepsilon(h)\\,dh=5\\varepsilon/16\\).  Since the posterior mean has no larger Bayes risk, rearrangement proves the first inequality.\n\nFor \\(\\Phi=\\phi_{c^\\dagger}\\), scaling\n\\(\\Phi_s(x)=s^{1/2}\\Phi(sx)\\) in the Airy Rayleigh quotient and differentiating at its minimum \\(s=1\\) gives\n\\[\n \\int|x|\\Phi(x)^2\\,dx\n =\\frac{2\\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}}{3\\kappa(c^\\dagger)}\n =\\frac{16}{15}\\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}.\n\\]\nThe weighted \\(H^1\\) convergence in the effective normalized Airy-record lemma and normalization of \\(w_k^\\dagger\\) imply\n\\(\\int|x|w_k^\\dagger\\to16\\Lambda_{c^\\dagger}/15\\).  Discarding the nonnegative transverse term gives the stated lower limit.",
    "justification": "This retained negative result isolates exactly why the two-coordinate scalar architecture fails and prevents its accidental reuse.",
    "gap": "It diagnoses only the scalar restriction; it is not an obstruction to the face-robust prior.",
    "consumer": "Supports the construction choice in the root theorem.",
